What makes you the perfect fit?To be eligible for this position you&hellip;
• Go the extra mile for our guests and your colleagues;
• Are flexible, friendly and an team player;
• Have good communication and social skills;
• Are fluent in English and/or Dutch, other languages are of course a plus. What do you get in return?The Amsterdam Marriott Hotel is part of Marriott International and offers a competitive salary & a wide package of benefits. Each year you will have a performance appraisal and depending on your performance you will get a salary increase. Furthermore we offer:
• Special discounted rates for 10.000+ Marriott hotels worldwide for you, your fam

Are you an avid cleaner or cleaner? Do you want to make sure that vacationing guests can start their vacation with a good feeling? Then read on quickly! 

We are looking for part-time cleaning employees for vacation park de Leistert in Roggel. Mondays and Fridays are the so-called changeover days when new guests arrive at the cottage. On these days it is important that the bungalows and vacation homes are cleaned properly. You do this with a whole team of enthusiastic and motivated cleaners. Together you make sure that everything looks spic and span. 

Tasks you will perform include:

- Making beds;
- Cleaning the kitchen, bathroom, bedroom and living room;
- Dusting and mopping everything; 
- Identifying defects and passing them on to the right people so that they can be repaired in a timely manner.

The work takes place on Mondays and Fridays between 9 a.m. and 3 p.m. Would you like to work more? Please let us know so we can discuss the possibilities! 

- You are a motivated cleaner who knows how to get things done;
- You speak the Dutch, English or German language;
- It is no problem to come to the location in Roggel (public transport is also possible); 
- You are available at least on Mondays and Fridays.

In the vacation periods it is always extra busy, it is important that you are flexible in these periods!

What will you do?

As an Operator, you will work in a dynamic production environment within the fresh produce industry (potatoes, vegetables, and fruit). You will play an important role in the sorting process of avocados and mangoes, ensuring that production runs smoothly and efficiently.

During your first week, you will work on the sorting line to gain a thorough understanding of the production process. You will sort fruit based on its ripeness while learning how the sorting department operates. After this onboarding period, you will be paired with an experienced buddy who will guide and support you until you are confident enough to work independently.

Your responsibilities include:

- Working on the sorting line during your onboarding period, sorting fruit based on ripeness;
- Receiving and processing production orders using the computer;
- Translating production orders into clear instructions for the sorting team;
- Supervising a sorting line of approximately 7 employees;
- Monitoring the quality and progress of the production process.

This is a varied role in which you will combine hands-on production work with team leadership. You will continuously switch between planning, execution, and coordinating your team to ensure production targets are met.

Working Days & Hours

You will work 38 hours per week, Monday through Friday, with occasional Saturdays when required.

Working hours: 06:45 AM – 03:30 PM, with occasional overtime until production has been completed.

- Available to work 38 hours per week, Monday through Friday (occasional Saturdays);
- Comfortable working with computers;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Experience in the fresh produce industry is an advantage;
- Experience as an Operator or in a supervisory role;
- Able to lead and motivate a team;
- Stress-resistant and able to adapt to changing circumstances.
